author ai
group render
note The element tree the whole GUI is built from: no widget objects, no retained state, no framework. Every frame the app opens and closes elements; each is nothing, text, or a custom draw function, and each has a size per axis that is exact, fits its content, or grows into what its parent has left. Nothing is positioned while the tree is being built - layout runs once at the end of the frame, five passes over the flat element list, and because a parent is always pushed before its children a forward walk is top-down and a reverse walk bottom-up. Input is answered from the previous frame's rectangles: an element with an id learns whether it is hovered, clicked or dragged one frame late, which is what lets the caller branch on a click in the same statement that creates the element. It knows nothing about codemap and nothing about wgpu; the renderer reaches it as one Measure for text and one Gfx to paint into.

