note Positions, top-down: an element's rectangle comes from the position its parent gave it, its clip is its parent's clip narrowed by the parent's own rectangle when the parent clips, and then it walks a cursor along its own direction placing its children, applying the cross-axis alignment and subtracting the scroll offset. The extent the cursor reached is stored as the content size, which is what the next frame clamps a scroll against.

