note Draw in tree order, layer 0 then layer 1, so a floating popup and everything inside it land on top - a child inherits its ancestors' layer first, which is what makes the contents of a popup rise with it. Per element: push its clip, fill, then text or the custom closure, then the borders. An element whose rectangle does not meet its clip is skipped outright.

